{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV10StyleColorV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"color","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inverted).","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLBarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/StyleColor":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StyleColor","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The bar-style-color type contains barline style and color information.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLBarline.StyleColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StyleColor","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/StyleColor/color":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor\/color","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor\/color","title":"color","abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"}}}